for regions that were stored in the CSMP nativefile format\&.

.PP
Using the connectivity indices for the \fBRegion\fP as retrieved from the CSMP++ native binary file and stored in \fBSubDomainInfo\fP, the regions are recreated\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
the numbering that is provided through the domain info must match the current state of the \fBMeshManager\fP\&.

.PP
the indices are just used to connect the element and node pointers of the region to the mesh storage, but, due to the sorting that this method will perform, they will not correspond to the indices used by the region accessors \fBN()\fP and \fBE()\fP\&.

.PP
this constructor initialises the data of the \fBModelSubDomain\fP from which the region is derived\&. This cannot be done by the subdomain itself because it does not know whether it will consist of elements, faces or interfaces\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
