.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::Region\fP< dim >::MoveNodeCoordinatesBy (const char * vector_variable)"

.PP
movement of the nodes in the region Displaces the node coordinates by displacements supplied as through the VECTOR variable (dim = dimensions of the model)\&. For each element, the nodes of which were displaced, the private boolean variable shape_to_date is set to false such that its volume is newly calculated once it is requested\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvector_variable\fP The name of the nodal \fBvector<double>\fP variable which holds the node coordinate displacement\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
After the assignment of the nodal displacements, \fBMoveNodeCoordinatesBy()\fP will set the \fBElement\fP state variable 'shape_to_data' to false\&. This will prompt re-calculation of elemental volumes if these are queried in subsequent computations\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
If a mesh shall be deformed using the diplacements of a deformation calculation stored in a \fBvector<double>\fP variable, ChangeNodeCoordinatesTo() can be used displace the node coordinates by these displacements\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
Due to the total garbage results that may arise, \fBMoveNodeCoordinatesBy()\fP will halt the simulation reporting a fatal error, if the target property is node a node or \fBvector<double>\fP type property\&. 
